;NO ELECTRON DENSITY WAS VISIBLE FOR THE RESIDUES 54-58, THEREFORE THE RESIDUES WERE BUILT STEREOCHEMICALLY, BUT THEIR OCCUPANCIES WERE SET TO ZERO. LOCALISATION OF TWO HETEROCOMPOUNDS (PHOSPHATES) INTO THE ELECTRON DENSITY. DOUBLE CONFORMATIONS COULD BE OBSERVED FOR THE FOLLOWING RESIDUE ATOMS: OG SER90, NZ LYS99, OG SER122, AND FOR THE ATOMS NE, CZ, NH1, NH2 OF ARG175. VAL79 SHOWS A TRIPLE CONFORMATION FOR ITS CG1 AND CG2 ATOMS.
;
